1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Tersmeden
2 CONT
2 CONT Vice-admiral Carl Tersmeden started his career as a naval officer in the Dutch and English navy, and sailed widely in his youth to the Caribbean, Portugal and Northern Africa. When war broke out again between Sweden and Russia he 
2 CONC served in the Gulf of Finland. After work had started on the fortress of Sveaborg outside Helsingfors, he supervised the building of the docks for the smaller vessels of the coastal fleet. For 15 years he worked here, and lived at
2 CONC  his country estate of Alberga in Esbo, which he bought in 1749. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On his promotion to the main naval base of Carlscrona in 1765 he left Alberga, and settled near his station. For his service to the crown he was ennobled, and named Vice-Admiral of the Naval Fleet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tersmeden was politically active, both locally in the parish of Esbo and on the national level as a member of Parliament. He was well connected both high and low. During his time at Sveaborg he registered as a burgher in Helsingfo
2 CONC rs, in order to do business, while at the same time being connected to the court of King Fredric through his mistress, Hedvig Taube, who was a childhood friend of Tersmeden's.
2 CONT
2 CONT The six published volumes of Carl Tersmeden's memoirs is an excerpt of his diary. The manuscript is 14 volumes in folio, totalling some 10761 numbered pages. The excerpt was published by Nils Erdman and Nils Sjöman 1912-1919. Even
2 CONC  the title stresses the publication's status as an excerpt: "Amiral Carl Tersmedens memoarer i sammandrag utgifna av Nils Erdman och Nils Sjöberg."
2 CONT
2 CONT The memoirs are a treasure trove to the cultural history of the XVIII:th century, and have been used as source material for numerous scholarly articles and books.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Tersmeden
