1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Brita lived on the farm at Ingesarven with her mother and father The farm had been in her grandmother's family since the early 1600's.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Her father died in 1816. In October 1820, at Ingesarven, Britta gave birth to a son Jonas.  In 1824 she gave birth to a son Anders in Högen which was about a mile away from Ingesarven; possibly she was working there as a maid. She
2 CONC  was not married at the time of either birth. In 1821 Nils Andersson Svard had moved from Fiskvik to Ingesarven but they were married in 1828. Possibly Nils was in the military during this period as well. It was not uncommon for c
2 CONC ouples to delay marriage several years after having children until they could afford it.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT It appears that Britta and Nils were very poor after her older brother got the family farm. In 1835 (and again in 1836) Brita was publicly punished for stealing (probably food for her family to eat). This was recorded in the churc
2 CONC h records and re-noted every year until 1861.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
